(Compile-fail: a call with no declared return type has nothing to be read as,
 so appending its result to a buffer is refused, as appending it to a list
 is. Plain, braced, and with no arguments, each used to write the address of
 the returned text.)

To 'untyped' of a text called word. Return "{word}?".
To 'no arguments'. Return "plain".
a buffer called other is 64 bytes in size.
append 'untyped' of "x" to other.
append {'untyped' of "y"} to other.
append 'no arguments' to other.
Print "top: {other}".
